# Run 2026-10-31, boot B1: fresh normal world (prep_srv.sh ... B spawn-animals=true spawn-monsters=true
# difficulty=normal), toml [named_mobs] chance = 1.0 before boot. Seed 8675309 (spawn area mostly ocean, so rows
# locate their biome and send the bot there). Locates go through the console: Async Locator answers later, hence
# waitlog + capture. Bot "qa" spawns in creative so a drop from y 200 does no damage.
pace 2

## SQ-B1-BOOT | boot clean, bot up
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (Mixin apply failed|InvalidInjectionException).*(creativeengineering|creative_delight)
bootreject \[named_mobs\].*(?i)warn
> pbot spawn qa 0 120 0 minecraft:overworld creative
> pbot status
expect ceperfbot ok

## SQ-GF31-04 | fresh world: next year is Year 2 at the first Early Spring (TI-37 server half, new row)
> cetime date
> cetime date next year
> cetime date
expect Year 2, Early Spring, day 1
> cetime date reset

## SQ-TD-01 | reset
> cetime date
# units are singular (day, month, season, year): `40 days` is refused (TI-32 and the queue wrote days)
> cetime date add 40 day
> cetime date reset
> cetime date
> time query daytime
expect Year 1, Early Spring, day 1 of 8, 7:42 am \(world day 1\)
expect The time is [0-9]{1,2}$
expect (?i)early spring

## SQ-TD-02 | next / previous / restart
> cetime date next month
> cetime date
> cetime date next month
> cetime date
> cetime date next month
> cetime date
> cetime date previous season
> cetime date
> cetime date add 3 day
> cetime date
> cetime date restart month
> cetime date
expect Mid Spring
expect Late Spring
expect Early Summer, day 1 of 8, 6:00 am
expect Early Spring, day 4
look order of the /cetime date answers: Mid Spring, Late Spring, Early Summer day 1 6:00 am, Early Spring day 1, Early Spring day 4, Early Spring day 1

## SQ-TD-03 | set an exact date, no double step
> cetime date set 3 mid_autumn 5 7:30 pm
> cetime date
> season
sleep 30
> cetime date
expect Year 3, Mid Autumn, day 5 of 8, 7:30 pm \(world day 253\)
count Mid Autumn, day 5 >= 2
expect (?i)mid autumn

## SQ-TD-04 | wine clock follows
> wine clock set 0 days
> cetime date add 1 month
> wine time
> cetime date add -1 month
> wine time
reject (?i)WARN.*(VintageClock|wine)
look wine time reads 8 days after the forward step and about 0 after the backward one; the chat line "wine clock moved back" goes to the console too

## SQ-TD-05 | every /cetime date change is logged
count \[time\] /cetime date >= 8

## SQ-NM-01 | naturally spawned cows, sheep, pigs get names (chance 1.0)
> execute positioned 3000 70 3000 run locate biome minecraft:plains
waitlog nearest minecraft:plains is at 300
capture PL is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> tp qa {PL1} 150 {PL3}
sleep 40
> execute at qa as @e[type=minecraft:cow,distance=..96] run data get entity @s CustomName
> execute at qa as @e[type=minecraft:sheep,distance=..96] run data get entity @s CustomName
> execute at qa as @e[type=minecraft:pig,distance=..96] run data get entity @s CustomName
> execute at qa as @e[type=minecraft:cow,distance=..96,limit=1] run data get entity @s ForgeData
> execute at qa as @e[type=minecraft:rabbit,distance=..96] run data get entity @s CustomName
reject Accessing LegacyRandomSource from multiple threads
expect creativeengineering:named_mob": 2b
look every cow/sheep/pig answer is a name ("has the following entity data"); rabbits "Found no elements"; no animals at all = locate plains from another far origin

## SQ-NM-02 | command spawns never roll
# a failed `data get` inside `execute as` prints nothing: tag the cow and read it directly
> execute at qa run summon minecraft:cow ~ ~ ~ {Tags:["qnm2"]}
> data get entity @e[tag=qnm2,limit=1] CustomName
expect Found no elements matching CustomName

## SQ-NM-03 | a named cow dies cleanly
> execute at qa run kill @e[type=minecraft:cow,limit=1,sort=furthest,distance=..96]
reject (?i)NamedMobs.*(exception|error)
expect (?i)named entity|died|was killed

## SQ-MG-18 | no chimpanzees in a jungle; gorillas forage Neapolitan bananas
> execute positioned 0 70 0 run locate biome minecraft:jungle
waitlog nearest minecraft:jungle is at 300
capture JG is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> tp qa {JG1} 200 {JG3}
sleep 20
repeat 10
> execute at qa run spreadplayers ~ ~ 1 24 false qa
> execute at qa run place feature neapolitan:banana_plant ~ ~ ~
end
> execute at qa run tp qa ~ ~ ~
> kill @e[type=neapolitan:chimpanzee]
> execute at qa run summon alexsmobs:gorilla ~2 ~ ~
> execute at qa run summon alexsmobs:gorilla ~-2 ~ ~
> execute at qa run summon alexsmobs:gorilla ~ ~ ~2
> time add 6000
sleep 120
> execute at qa if entity @e[type=item,nbt={Item:{id:"alexsmobs:banana"}},distance=..48]
> execute at qa if entity @e[type=item,nbt={Item:{id:"neapolitan:banana"}},distance=..48]
expect No entity was found
look the chimp kill finds nothing; the alexsmobs banana check fails and the neapolitan one passes (if neither, gorillas did not forage in 2 min: zq count leaves near qa, wait longer); spreadplayers moves the bot across the canopy
# `if entity ...nbt` and `place feature` left no log line on 10-31 B1: data get probes instead
> execute at qa run tp qa ~ ~ ~
sleep 1
capture QA Teleported qa to (-?\d+)\.\d+, (-?\d+)\.\d+, (-?\d+)
> zq count {QA1-32} {QA2-40} {QA3-32} {QA1+32} {QA2+20} {QA3+32} neapolitan:banana_stalk
> execute at qa as @e[type=minecraft:item,distance=..48] run data get entity @s Item.id
> execute at qa as @e[type=alexsmobs:gorilla,distance=..48] run data get entity @s HandItems
reject alexsmobs:banana
look at least one neapolitan:banana among the item ids or hands; banana_stalk count above 0 (plants placed)
sleep 3

