## SQ-MCL-05 | forced level 2: no new monster more than 32 blocks above or below the player
# needs [perf] mobCapForceLevel = 2 set in the toml BEFORE the boot (a running server does not reload the toml);
# run on its own restart (A2: after a2_variants; B1: on the B1b boot), then set it back to -1
> pbot spawn qm {PL1} 120 {PL3} minecraft:overworld survival
# fresh boot: nothing spawns near a just-joined bot for about 2.5 min (10-31): wait it out
sleep 160
> time set 18000
> kill @e[type=#zq:monsters]
sleep 120
> execute at qm as @e[type=#zq:monsters,distance=..128] run data get entity @s Pos[1]
> execute at qm run data get entity qm Pos[1]
look every monster Y within 32 of qm's Y; qm stands in plains over caves
> pbot remove qm
> time set noon

